narrative:
## Making Text SHOUT and whisper

XIOM gives you two handy functions for changing how text looks: `string.str_upper()` makes everything BIG, and `string.str_lower()` makes everything small.

### Transforming Text

```xiom
fn main() {
  let message: Str = "Hello World";
  let loud: Str = string.str_upper(message);
  let quiet: Str = string.str_lower(message);
  io.println(loud);
  io.println(quiet);
}
```

This prints `HELLO WORLD` on one line and `hello world` on the next. Notice that letters change case but spaces and punctuation stay exactly the same!

### Why Would You Do This?

Ever logged into a website and typed your email in all caps by accident? Many programs automatically convert usernames to lowercase so "CoolKid123" and "coolkid123" match. It's also great for making titles, formatting names, or creating fun text effects.

### Combining with Other Skills

```xiom
fn main() {
  let name: Str = "alex";
  let upper_name: Str = string.str_upper(name);
  let greeting: Str = string.str_concat("HELLO ", upper_name);
  io.println(greeting);
}
```

We uppercase the name, then use concat to build a greeting. Now the whole message shouts: `HELLO ALEX`!

